description:
Found by the s525q binder dual-run over the GATE (PCL_BINDER_CHECK=log PCL_BINDER_LOG=... tools/prove-core): the program of Pl/t/sig-param-shadow-01.t's row "a DIFFERENT-sigil use of the same bare name is still a capture" -- `_block_captures_name` (via _sub_captures_name < _check_sub_captures < parse) answers 1 (sub g captures the file lexical `@x`); the binder (pad.c) answers 0: `my @x` is declared AFTER `sub g`, so inside g `@x` is the GLOBAL @main::x (intro_my: a `my` is visible from the next statement; a named sub's body is compiled where it is written).

Probe (scratch/s525q/probes/H1.pl in the s525q worktree):

    use feature "signatures";
    sub g ($x) { "g($x)[@x]" }
    my @x = (7, 8);
    print g(1), "\n";

perl 5.40.3:  g(1)[]
base (main 81ef05e5):  Transpile failed: / Parser2 TODO: file lexical 'x' captured by sub g   -- a LOUD refusal of valid perl (no wrong value).
Control H2.pl (no signature: `sub g { "g[@x]" } my @x = (7, 8); @main::x = (1); print g()`): base prints g[1] = perl, so the plain capture check IS position-aware; the signature-parameter path (#454's `_signature_param_canons` narrowing) is what counts the LATER `my @x`.

NOTE for the fixer: Pl/t/sig-param-shadow-01.t:122-136 ASSERTS this refusal and its comment says the body's `@x` "is the file's `my @x` -- a genuine capture"; per perl it is not (perl prints g(1)[]).  Fixing the check means rewriting that row under the s377 four-conjunct expectation rule (perl-probed text, the diff = exactly the divergence, the edit STRENGTHENS, a guard row in the same commit) -- e.g. assert the program runs and prints `g(1)[]`, and keep a refusal row for a `my @x` declared BEFORE the sub.

Belongs to 1c (the capture-gate port asks the binder's `captures`, which is positional by construction).  NOT fixed in s525q (inert batch).
